oken, while ChatGPT generates 40 tokens on average), resulting in inflated str-em scores."},{"id":"c34","chunkId":"743155d9b0541c99_c_23c79895493f4fa2","docId":"743155d9b0541c99","docTitle":"2401.15391_MultiHop_RAG_Benchmarking_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Multi_Hop","page":7,"quote":"Models Accuracy Retrieved Chunk Ground-truth Chunk GPT-4 0.56 0.89 ChatGPT 0.44 0.57 Llama-2-70b-chat-hf 0.28 0.32 Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct 0.32 0.36 Claude-2.1 0.52 0.56 Google-PaLM 0.47 0.74 Table 6: Generation accuracy of LLMs."},{"id":"c35","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_e2936d52a59d465f","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":18,"quote":"Our findings revealed that text-davinci-003 has the highest number of missing passages, totaling 280 instances. ChatGPT also misses a considerable number of passages, occurring 153 times."},{"id":"c36","chunkId":"d2068edc08df316d_c_44b30e3207fc89ad","docId":"d2068edc08df316d","docTitle":"Siren's Song in the AI Ocean: A Survey on Hallucination in Large Language Models","page":28,"quote":"Chatgpt be- yond english: Towards a comprehensive evalu- ation of large language models in multilingual learning."},{"id":"c37","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_39534a0769e834f0","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":6,"quote":"We also compare four LLMs provided Method nDCG@1 nDCG@5 nDCG@10 BM25 54.26 52.78 50.58 gpt-3.5-turbo 82.17 71.15 65.80 Initial passage order (1) Random order 26.36 25.32 25.17 (2) Reverse order 36.43 31.79 32.77 Number of re-ranking (3)"},{"id":"c38","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_12e8858fc6e24b99","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":18,"quote":"The findings turn out that ChatGPT and GPT-4 are more consistent in ranking passages compared to the Davinci model. GPT-4 also slightly outperforms ChatGPT in terms of the RBO metric."},{"id":"c39","chunkId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459_c_eec1b2c45749e73b","docId":"737b0b8fe0aa8459","docTitle":"2501.00309_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_with_Graphs_GraphRAG","page":22,"quote":"M-based verbalizing works better for ChatGPT while template-based works better for LLaMA [398]."},{"id":"c40","chunkId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17_c_3796676205cbf32f","docId":"3a2ca388b4a2fb17","docTitle":"2304.09542_Is_ChatGPT_Good_at_Search_Investigating_Large_Language_Models_as_Re_Ra","page":1,"quote":"Finally, to im- prove efficiency in real-world applications, we delve into the potential for distilling the rank- ing capabilities of ChatGPT into small special- ized models using a permutation distillation scheme."},{"id":"c41","chunkId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f_c_589bc4e8cae01e02","docId":"396a0fadeb4cd40f","docTitle":"2312.10997_Retrieval_Augmented_Generation_for_Large_Language_Models_A_Survey","page":2,"quote":"OVERVIEW OF RAG A typical application of RAG is illustrated in Figure 2. Here, a user poses a question to ChatGPT about a recent, widely discussed news."},{"id":"c42","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_0e32f47392d44c61","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":12,"quote":"A Implementation Details A.1 Models and Infrastructures Details We use two OpenAI models, GPT-3.5-turbo and GPT-4 (sizes currently unknown), and an open- source model, Mistral-7b (7 billion parameters)."},{"id":"c43","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_15c46938e05da486","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Knowledge_Graph","page":7,"quote":"Comparing the LLMs, GPT-4 emerges as the top performer, with Mistral-7b and GPT-3.5-turbo exhibiting comparable results."},{"id":"c44","chunkId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3_c_36f42e6c927e3d4a","docId":"01d82c67ac18ffc3","docTitle":"2404.03868_Extract_Define_Canonicalize_An_LLM_based_Framework_for_Know